From: Armada contributors <noreply@armada-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: es8326: add the vddio supply

Adapted from armada (armada-os/armada b91b786) 1176, itself from
RetroidPocket/linux f8dfc9104b7c, plus the es8326 part of armada 1177
(binding, from RetroidPocket/linux e192bf797bdb).

armada enables "vdd" and "vddio" together with
devm_regulator_bulk_get_enable(). Our `0842` already takes an optional
"vdd", cut across suspend; this adds "vddio" next to it, optional and on
for as long as the device is bound. The Retroid Pocket Duo wires vdd to a
3.3 V and vddio to a 1.8 V GPIO-switched rail. Boards without a vddio
supply are unaffected.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml | 6 ++++++
 sound/soc/codecs/es8326.c                                   | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml
index b5594a9d5..c7719a122 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/everest,es8326.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,12 @@ properties:
   "#sound-dai-cells":
     const: 0
 
+  vdd-supply:
+    description: Analog and digital core supply (AVDD/DVDD)
+
+  vddio-supply:
+    description: I/O supply
+
   everest,jack-pol:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8
     description: |
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/es8326.c b/sound/soc/codecs/es8326.c
index 07678746b..2082c1765 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/es8326.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/es8326.c
@@ -1348,6 +1348,11 @@ static int es8326_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	if (!es8326)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/* I/O rail: on for as long as the device is bound, kept across suspend */
+	ret = devm_regulator_get_enable_optional(&i2c->dev, "vddio");
+	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
+		return dev_err_probe(&i2c->dev, ret, "failed to enable vddio supply\n");
+
 	es8326->vdd = devm_regulator_get_optional(&i2c->dev, "vdd");
 	if (IS_ERR(es8326->vdd)) {
 		if (PTR_ERR(es8326->vdd) != -ENODEV)
